  "notes": "Cash-basis village with accrual-basis water/sewer funds. Governmental lines from p4 (Total column); business-type from p6 (proprietary revenues, expenses, changes in net position, Total column); business_type measure = net position. Donations 3,000 are printed under Other financing sources on p4, so placed in other_financing. Transfers net (10,544) governmental out, +10,543 business-type in. Debt service 0 line skipped. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (p1); p1 prints a single Long-term debt 315,000, split here per p5 (75,000 current portion / 240,000 bonds payable; p5 also prints AP 27,803 vs p1 27,802). Governmental ending 725,674 per p4 (p3 prints 725,673). Detail: General Fund revenue from the p8 budget schedule; General Fund expenditures from the p11 combining schedule Total column (object lines, more detailed than the p8 function totals, which are not recorded to avoid double counting; p11 revenue not recorded; budget_final null because p8 budget lines are function totals that do not match p11 object lines). p11 expenditure lines add to 1,375,301 vs printed 1,375,300 (recorded in report_discrepancies); p11 spending is by object so function categories are guesses (review). p8 public safety 112,738 and culture 301,187 differ from statement p4 because public buildings 61,170 is reallocated there; p8 revenue includes donations 3,000 which p4 shows as other financing. Dashes in budget columns recorded as null. Proprietary budget schedule p10 (cash/budget basis, utility sales 649,050 vs 647,580 on p6) recorded as detail; its lines add to 637,805 / 659,936 vs printed totals 637,804 / 659,935 (rounding). Proprietary Statement of Cash Flows (p7) not recorded in proprietary field because basis is not GAAP; its totals: operating 89,010, noncapital 10,543, capital -77,765, investing 343, cash 675,874 to 698,072. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
